 "equipment_type": "Boiler burner management system (LMV2x/3x) via ProtoAir gateway",
 "applies_to": "Thermal Solutions and Bryan boilers fired by a Siemens LMV2x or LMV3x burner management system, connected to the Universal Gateway (ProtoAir FPA-W44).",
 "summary": "The ProtoAir Universal Gateway reads a Siemens LMV2x/3x burner management system over Modbus and serves it on BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP. It reports burner phase, actuator positions, VSD output, fuel and output, flame signal, counters, the current error and an error history entry, and splits the input and output status words into binary objects (safety loop, pressure switches, alarm, ignition, fan, fuel valves). The BMS can write program stop, Modbus mode and timeout, remote operating mode and target output.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "The table has no read/write column; AV objects (N2 analog outputs) are taken as writable. BV 1 Com Status is a status point and is listed as read.",
  "Several AV objects are resettable counters or burner settings (hours run, start counters, fuel volume, preselected outputs); write them only on purpose.",
  "Binary objects named Inputs Word n / Outputs Word n are unnamed bits of the status words, as printed.",
  "The manual gives no units, ranges or state texts for this profile; see the Siemens LMV2x/3x Modbus documentation."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "Universal Gateway Instruction Manual (ProtoAir): BACnet MS/TP, BACnet IP, N2, Modbus",
  "doc_number": "PN 106417-04 Rev A",
  "revision_date": "2024-05",
  "url": "https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/catsy.782/Universal+Gateway+ProtoAir+BACnet+Instruction+Manual.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Add the LMV2_3 profile in the ProtoAir Web Configurator with a unique Node-ID and discover it at 50000 + Node-ID. Read burner phase, current output, flame signal, alarm and the current error code. For remote control set Modbus mode to remote and write the remote operating mode and target output, checking the Modbus breakdown time setting (AV 16).",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "AV 15",
    "name": "Modbus mode",
    "why": "Local or remote (Modbus/BMS) operation"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 17",
    "name": "Operating mode in remote op",
    "why": "Operating mode while in remote operation"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 18",
    "name": "Preselect target output mod/multistg",
    "why": "Target output (firing rate) in remote operation"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 1",
    "name": "Burner control phase",
    "why": "Burner sequence phase"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 6",
    "name": "Current output",
    "why": "Current burner output"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 7",
    "name": "Flame signal",
    "why": "Flame signal"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BI 17",
    "name": "Alarm",
    "why": "Burner alarm output"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 10",
    "name": "Current error: Error code",
    "why": "Current error code"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 1",
    "name": "Com Status",
    "why": "Modbus link between ProtoAir and the LMV"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "AV 15 Modbus mode selects local or remote (Modbus) operation; in remote the LMV uses AV 17 and AV 18. The manual does not list the values.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "Device instance = Node_Offset (default 50,000) + the controller's Node-ID (1-255), so Node-ID 1 gives 50001.",
   "ProtoAir default IP address is 192.168.1.24, mask 255.255.255.0.",
   "Add each controller as a profile in the ProtoAir Web Configurator and give it a unique Node-ID."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Hours-run, start-counter and fuel-volume AVs are resettable counters; do not write them cyclically.",
   "No state texts are printed for Modbus mode or the operating mode; check the Siemens documentation.",
   "AV 16 Modbus breakdown time is a timeout setting; the manual gives no default or behaviour for it."
  ]
 },
